      "hints": [
        "Form quadratic $mx^2 + cx - 16 = 0$.",
        "Set discriminant $\\Delta = c^2 + 64m = 0$.",
        "Express $m$ in terms of $c$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute $y = mx + c$ into the curve equation $xy = 16$ to form a quadratic in $x$:\n$$x(mx + c) = 16 \\implies mx^2 + cx - 16 = 0$$",
        "Set the discriminant $b^2 - 4ac = 0$ for tangency:\n$$c^2 - 4(m)(-16) = 0 \\implies c^2 + 64m = 0$$",
        "Solve for $m$ in terms of $c$:\n$$64m = -c^2 \\implies m = -\\frac{c^2}{64}$$"
      ],
